<!-- ============ ARTICLE ============ -->
<article class="article">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead-para">
        While working in a clinic as an orthotist and prosthetist, I witnessed a
        recurring challenge that deeply stayed with me. Many amputees, after
        receiving their prosthetic limbs, were eager to return to daily life — but
        they often felt unprepared for the realities they would face outside the
        clinic.
      </p>

      <p>
        There was a clear gap between clinical care and real-world experience.
        Patients had questions, concerns, and uncertainties that extended far
        beyond their appointments, yet they lacked an <strong>accessible, reliable
        source of support.</strong> This observation inspired me to take action.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="grad">A place built on trust and accessibility</span></h2>

      <p>
        I created a small-scale online platform designed specifically for
        prosthetic users — a place where amputees could seek guidance, ask
        questions, and feel supported in their day-to-day lives. Through this
        website, I provided personalised consultations, addressing their concerns
        about using prosthetic limbs in real-life situations.
      </p>

      <p>The platform was built on two simple commitments:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Users could reach out with their questions and receive expert guidance, directly from a clinician who understood their devices.</li>
        <li>If technical issues arose, I connected them with a prosthetist colleague for specialised support.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        While consultations themselves were <strong>free</strong>, I received a
        small commission from technical referrals — which helped sustain the
        platform and its maintenance without putting a price on a patient's first
        question.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Stats band -->
    <div class="story-stats">
      <div class="story-stat">
        <div class="v">Free</div>
        <div class="l">Consultations for every prosthetic user who reached out</div>
